 "placement": [
  "Electrodes: two metal pads on the case where both thumbs or hands rest (LA, RA) give a 2-electrode configuration with ac lead-off (p19 fig 51; RLD then biases the inputs, p17). A third electrode (RL) improves mains rejection: a third pad, or a small dedicated 3-pin connector.",
  "The bench header's eight lines go through the SN74AXC8T245 shifter and are digital: electrodes CANNOT use them. Electrodes through the header need three extra analogue pins wired straight to the 180k/360k resistors.",
  "Input traces symmetrical and length-matched, safety and bias resistors placed identically for both inputs (p20); keep the 10M nodes short and away from the e-paper and converter switching nodes.",
  "Medical-safety note (p25): demonstration circuit only. Use only while running from the battery, never while USB is connected to a mains charger."
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Configuration: Fig 66 'cardiac monitor' (p25): 0.5 Hz two-pole high-pass, 40 Hz two-pole low-pass, gain 100 x 11 = 1100, third electrode driven. Fig 67 shows about 61 dB pass band.",
  "Output into the 1.8 V ADC: REFOUT = VS/2 = 1.65 V and OUT can reach VS-0.1 V when the inputs saturate (lead-off), so OUT is halved: 0.05-1.6 V at the pin, centred at 0.83 V. Never above 1.65 V even with +VS at 3.3 V.",
  "Safety resistors: datasheet rule is VS / 10 uA (p19, p23); at 3.3 V that is 330k for one resistor. The fig 66 values (180k + 180k in the LA-RA path, 360k on RL) meet it for the series path [interpretation]."
 ],
